  "transcript": {
    "heloc-five-years.mp4": "Five years of HELOC payments, and the balance is still $50,000. That happens when you pay only the interest. A federal survey found more than a quarter of HELOC holders mostly do. And 62% of them expected to pay it off within five years. But an interest-only payment puts nothing toward the balance. The months go by, and the number sits there. So what would five years take? That's about $833 a month toward the balance, plus interest on top. So check your last statement. If the balance didn't drop, you don't have a payoff date yet. Message me, and we'll work one out that fits your budget. Or keep paying just the interest, and in five years, you're right back here."
